{"raw": {"https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4786": {"title": "Accounts Payable Clerk", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Accounts Payable Clerk Department/Faculty Finance Home Campus (Location) Langley, BC Employment Duration 12 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4786 Internal Closing Date: August 30, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 6 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $27.91 to $31.16 per hour Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Hours of Work (BCGEU): 8:30am-4:30pm Hours per Week (BCGEU): 35 We are currently seeking an Accounts Payable Clerk to join our Finance team. Job Overview To ensure documentation submitted to the Finance database complies with established accounting principles and University policies and procedures. Education and Experience Good working knowledge of English (written and verbal). Completion of the first year of an accounting/business program supplemented with approximately three years related experience or equivalent combination of education and experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated working knowledge of integrated finance accounting systems. Demonstrated knowledge of common PC applications software such as spreadsheet, database and word processing. Proven ability to communicate courteously and effectively in person, in writing and over the telephone with a diverse range of individuals. Demonstrated ability to recognize, analyze and resolve problems. Demonstrated ability to compose routine and non-routine correspondence and reports. Demonstrated ability to work independently, establish priorities and meet deadlines. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4835": {"title": "Admissions Coordinator", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Admissions Coordinator Department/Faculty Student Services - Registrar's Office Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 18 Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4835 Internal Closing Date: October 9, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 13 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $33.88 to $37.81 per hour Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Hours of Work (BCGEU): 8:30am - 4:30pm Hours per Week (BCGEU): 35 We are currently seeking an Admissions Coordinator to join our Office of the Registrar team. Job Overview To plan, organize and evaluate student services in the Office of the Registrar, and to coordinate student admission and transfer credit procedures that directly influence the impact of student services regarding admission, registration and retention of students across all Kwantlen campuses. Education and Experience A minimum of five (5) years\u2019 experience in progressively responsible administrative support positions preferably in an Office of the Registrar at a post-secondary institution, including at least three (3) years\u2019 experience in a supervisory position. A minimum of two (2) years of post-secondary education or an equivalent combination of education and experience. \u00a0Bachelor\u2019s degree is preferred. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Formal training and/or extensive acquired knowledge in computing, including high level proficiency using BANNER Student, or a similar student records-based system and Microsoft Office. Demonstrated exceptional customer service skills, including dealing effectively with a diverse range of people and situations. Experience monitoring a telephone/call system. Experience overseeing admissions processes, including demonstrated knowledge of transfer credit, for domestic and international applicants. Familiarity with international admissions, foreign credential evaluation, and various education systems as well as immigration policies. Experience in planning and presenting training activities. Experience in developing and administering employee performance standards, and conducting performance appraisals. Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal, including experience in public speaking. Demonstrated analytical skills, including problem-solving and needs analysis. Excellent organizational skills, including the ability to multi-task, set priorities and meet strict deadlines. Ability to work independently, exercise good judgment and demonstrate initiative. Ability to develop flexible approaches toward work procedures and to improvise satisfactory alternatives as required. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with University administration, faculty, staff and students. Aptitude for exacting and precise work. Knowledge of University programs and courses and demonstrated ability to keep up to date with credit, non-credit and continuing education University offerings, University and program admissions, transfer credit and registration policies, tuition fees, timetable changes, class cancellations etc. Full command of the English language, both written and oral. Second language an asset. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4724": {"title": "AGC Research Technician", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description AGC Research Technician Department/Faculty Applied Genomics Centre Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration Until March 31, 2027 Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4724 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Director, Applied Genomics Centre. SUMMARY The Research Technician has a supportive role for research goals of the Applied Genomics Centre (AGC). This individual will support applied research projects under the supervision and direction of the AGC Director, Laboratory and Research Coordinator, and senior research staff. Where appropriate, they may also help supervise and train student researchers working in the AGC laboratories, or in the field as applicable. They will contribute to experimental design, perform laboratory tasks, and communicate results to the Director, Associates, and industry partners. There are currently 2 openings for this position. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Provide research support for the AGC\u2019s Director, Faculty project leads, Laboratory and Research Coordinator, and senior research staff Gather, organize and maintain experimental data and records in the AGC lab, and in the field when required Execute experiments required for research projects, including quality control, and troubleshooting when necessary Assist in preparing reports and presentations, collaboratively and under the direction of the AGC\u2019s senior leadership Provide on-site supervision and training to undergraduate student researchers, when required Generate and update standard operating procedures for routine and new developments, in collaboration with the Laboratory and Research Coordinator and/or senior research staff Other duties as assigned QUALIFICATIONS BSc in Biology or related discipline Relevant experience with a focus on genomics and/or metabolomics Research experience is an asset *SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $24.00 - $28.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4791": {"title": "Appliance Servicing Instructor", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Appliance Servicing Instructor Department/Faculty Faculty of Trades & Technology Home Campus (Location) Cloverdale Tech - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 1 (one) year on call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4791 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 3 *Salary Information: Faculty Pay Scale Employment Type: Qualified Faculty List Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Faculty (Kwantlen Faculty Association) Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): APPLIANCE SERVICE TECHNICIAN INSTRUCTOR POSITION TYPE: QUALIFIED FACULTY LIST POSITION START: As soon as possible FACULTY OVERVIEW: The Appliance Service Technician program prepares students for entry into the appliance service and repair industry. Students complete all of the in-school training required for Red Seal qualifications and develop their skills through hands-on opportunities. Students also acquire a sound knowledge of common appliance systems and essential skills necessary to succeed in the industry. POSITION OVERVIEW: The Faculty of Trades and Technology is currently seeking a Non-regular Type 1 Appliance Service Technician Instructor to provide short-term coverage in the Appliance Service Technician program which may extend from a single day to several weeks, possibly leading to a regularized contract. Part of this contract may require the delivery of the BC Provincial Appliance Service Technician Gas Certificate. More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: A BC Certificate of Qualification (BC TQ), or a Certificate of Qualification with Interprovincial Red Seal (IP RSE) from another jurisdiction. A BC Gas Certificate, or equivalent. A minimum of five years relevant, related, industry experience as an Appliance Service Journeyperson. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates will be required to undergo a Criminal Record Check. *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. This competition is for successful candidates to be added to our Qualified Faculty List. When work in this area becomes available, the Qualified Faculty List will be drawn upon to assign work. As such, please indicate on your application your preferred workload percentage. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4744": {"title": "Artist in Residence", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Artist in Residence Department/Faculty Faculty of Arts Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration 3-6 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4744 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: On-Call Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Associate Dean or designate. SUMMARY The Faculty of Arts invites applications from the KPU Entertainment Arts Alumni or current Entertainment Arts students for 1-4 positions as Artist in Residence. These residencies will work on projects initiated by KPU groups the KPU Creative Lab and collaborate with current Entertainment Arts students in creating content to develop, promote, and communicate the identified projects led by faculty. They will help contribute materials and assets to projects, attend meetings, and complete work as assigned related to the KPU Creative Lab. Working schedules for the Artist(s) in Residence may be flexible over the course of the project durations. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Attend weekly planning sessions with the faculty project lead as required Assist and elicit support from members to scope, plan, and execute their projects Work on assigned topics and tasks within the scope of the projects Provide/receive feedback to and from their project members Adhere to the Policies and Procedures of the university Establish and maintain effective relationships with administrators, peers, support staff, students and the community at large Participate in scheduled meetings and appropriate university-related activities as requested by the Dean or designate. QUALIFICATIONS Education and Experience Demonstrable familiarity and experience in one or more of the following disciplines: 3D Animation/3D Modelling VFX Game Development Graduated or current student from KPU Entertainment Arts Advanced VFX Program, Advanced 3D Animation and 3D Modelling Program, or Game Development Program Experience working in the industry and with students is advantageous Skills and Abilities Excellent communication, organizational, time management and interpersonal skills Critical thinking and problem-solving skills Ability to interpret and apply university, government, agency and departmental policies, procedures, and guidelines Ability to exercise a high level of initiative and responsibility Ability to use tact and discretion to deal with or settle complex requests Ability to communicate effectively and efficiently SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $45.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4773": {"title": "Associate Dean, Faculty of Trades and Technology", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Associate Dean, Faculty of Trades and Technology Department/Faculty Faculty of Trades & Technology Home Campus (Location) Cloverdale Tech - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 5 years Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4773 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 14 \u2013 Administrative Salary Grid - $114,071 to $174,909 Employment Type: Permanent Full Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Administration/Management Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): The Opportunity Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is seeking a collaborative and experienced Associate Dean to join the leadership team within the Faculty of Trades and Technology. Reporting to the Dean, Faculty of Trades and Technology, the Associate Dean provides strategic, administrative, and educational leadership across a diverse range of departments and disciplines. Working closely with the Dean, the Director, Strategy and Business Development, and other administrative leaders, you will help advance the Faculty\u2019s academic priorities while supporting excellence in programs, curriculum, teaching, and the student experience. You will bring a strong understanding of the BC trades training system, a commitment to academic excellence, and the ability to navigate complex operational, employee, and student matters in a collaborative and solutions-focused manner. As Associate Dean, Faculty of Trades and Technology, you will: Lead, coach, and support direct reports, including the Coordinator, Program Inventory and Support, by setting shared goals, guiding performance, and fostering a collaborative and respectful culture. Contribute to positive employee and labour relations by administering collective agreements, representing management in grievance processes, and consulting with Human Resources on interpretation and processes. Engage departments in collaborative long-term planning to advance Faculty and University objectives. Provide leadership and shared oversight for academic programs and curriculum, including curriculum development, program review, revisions, and the facilitation of program changes. Monitor faculty workload assignments, course offerings, enrolment patterns, and projections to support effective academic planning and resource allocation. Lead Faculty recruitment and hiring processes, chair faculty and staff search committees, and support the orientation, retention, evaluation, and assignment of employees. Respond to and resolve student complaints, appeals, academic integrity matters, and other complex student issues in accordance with University and Faculty policies. Review and oversee processes related to academic waivers and substitutions, transfer credit, independent study, and prior learning assessment. Participate in the development and monitoring of the Faculty\u2019s budget, approve expenditures as a designate of the Dean, and support responsible resource management. Work with the Dean\u2019s office, faculty, staff, and the Occupational Health and Safety Committee to support effective communication and coordination of health and safety matters. Represent the Faculty on departmental, divisional, University, and external committees, councils, and community bodies. Model high standards of service, accountability, professional practice, and continuous learning through assigned duties, education, and training. Promote and maintain a safe, equitable, respectful, and inclusive work environment grounded in University policies, procedures, and mandatory training. What You Bring You are an experienced academic leader who understands the opportunities and complexities of delivering high-quality trades and technology education in a post-secondary environment. You bring a collaborative and supportive leadership style, sound judgment, and the ability to balance strategic priorities with day-to-day academic and operational demands. Your communication skills, relationship-building approach, and commitment to academic and service excellence enable you to work effectively with faculty, staff, students, senior leaders, unions, and external partners. You are comfortable addressing complex issues, making thoughtful decisions, and guiding teams through change while maintaining a culture of respect and accountability. We\u2019re looking for someone who: Holds a master\u2019s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and experience. Brings at least five years of teaching experience in a post-secondary environment, including significant committee experience. Has demonstrated success in a leadership role with progressively increasing responsibility; experience as a Department Head, Chair, Associate Dean, or in a similar post-secondary academic leadership role is preferred. Has a fundamental understanding of the BC trades training system. Demonstrates knowledge of trades and technology programs and a strong commitment to academic excellence and the student learning experience. Understands academic programs, curriculum, faculty workload, enrolment planning, and faculty management processes. Has experience hiring, mentoring, coaching, and building leadership capacity among faculty and staff. Demonstrates strong interpersonal and communication skills and a record of developing effective working relationships. Can analyze complex situations, exercise sound judgment, and develop practical and effective solutions. Is able to work effectively under pressure, manage competing priorities, and resolve sensitive or complex matters. Brings strong organizational skills and the ability to manage academic, operational, and logistical responsibilities. Has experience working in a teaching-intensive post-secondary institution and a unionized academic environment; both are considered assets. Fosters a supportive, respectful, collaborative, and inclusive working environment. The Location KPU is a multi-campus institution. \u00a0The Trades and Technology offices are located on the Cloverdale campus, however, frequent travel between campuses will be required. Want to know more? Click here to view the full job description. Application Process To apply for this opportunity, please submit your cover letter and resume as one document via KPU\u2019s Career Centre. \u00a0Resume review will be conducted on October 12, 2026; however, the competition will remain open until filled. For inquiries or recommendations related to this position, please contact: Evita Gandhi Talent Acquisition Specialist Email: evita.gandhi@kpu.ca Salary Information The above compensation range is the span between the minimum and maximum base salary for a position.\u00a0\u00a0Typically, initial salary placement is approximately halfway between the minimum and the maximum.\u00a0\u00a0This represents an employee that possesses full job knowledge, qualifications and experience for the position.\u00a0\u00a0In the normal course, employees will be hired, transferred or promoted between the minimum and approximately halfway of the salary range for a job with consideration given to internal equity. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4832": {"title": "Carpentry Instructor", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Carpentry Instructor Department/Faculty Faculty of Trades & Technology Home Campus (Location) Cloverdale Tech - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 4 weeks Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4832 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Faculty Pay Scale Employment Type: Faculty Contract Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Faculty (Kwantlen Faculty Association) Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): CARPENTRY INSTRUCTOR POSITION TYPE: NR 1 (Non-Regular Type 1) POSITION START: To Be Announced KPU proudly offers all learners opportunities to achieve success in a diverse range of programs that blend theory and practice, critical understanding, and social and ethical awareness necessary for good citizenship and rewarding careers. FACULTY OVERVIEW: The Faculty of Trades & Technology at Kwantlen Polytechnic University is currently seeking a Non-Regular Type 1 (contract) Carpentry/Building Construction instructor to provide short-term delivery of entry level and apprenticeship training, which may extend from a single day to several weeks. POSITION OVERVIEW: The delivery of this four-week program will take place in-person in Campbell River, BC. More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum qualifications include a Certificate of Qualification with Interprovincial Red Seal Endorsement (IP RSE). A minimum of five years current industry experience as a Carpentry/Building Construction Journeyperson. Also required is the knowledge and ability to communicate effectively with students. Preference will be given to those applicants with a demonstrated record of teaching successfully, current carpentry skills and five (5) years supervisory or administrative experience. Contract consideration may be subject to a practical assessment. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates will be required to undergo a Criminal Record Check. *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. The successful candidate of this competition may be added to our Qualified Faculty List. When work in this area becomes available, the Qualified Faculty List will be drawn upon to assign work. As such, please indicate on your application your preferred workload percentage. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4664": {"title": "Director, Student Access and Disability Resources", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Director, Student Access and Disability Resources Department/Faculty Student Services - Accessibility Services Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration Permanent Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4664 Internal Closing Date: October 30, 2026 External Closing Date: October 30, 2026 # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 14 \u2013 Administrative Salary Grid - $114,071 to $174,909 Employment Type: Permanent Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Administration/Management Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): We are currently seeking a Director, Student Access and Disability Resources to join our Student Affairs team. Job Overview The Director, Student Access and Disability Resources reports to the Associate Vice-President, Student Affairs. Reporting directly to this position is the Manager, Accessibility Services, the Manager, Assessment and Testing Services, and Learning Specialists (faculty). The Director, Student Access and Disability Resources provides strategic and institutional leadership for Accessibility Services and Assessment & Testing Services. The Director is accountable for advancing the University\u2019s commitment to substantive equality and inclusive access for students with disabilities and for students and community members who access assessment and testing services. The Director leads the development and integration of university-wide strategies to identify, prevent, and remove systemic barriers affecting students\u2019 access to post-secondary education, and to ensure the duty to accommodate students with disabilities is met through the coordinated delivery of accessible accommodations, assessments, and testing services across multiple campuses. The Director provides senior oversight of complex student needs, government- and university-funded resources, risk management, and compliance related to student access and assessment. The Director represents the University in partnerships with students, faculty, community organizations, and provincial and federal bodies to strengthen accountability, accessibility, and continuous improvement of student-centred services. Education and Experience A Master\u2019s Degree in a related field; Minimum of 7 years\u2019 experience working in progressively responsible roles, in postsecondary student services; A minimum of 5 years\u2019 management experience leading and supervising staff in a postsecondary setting; Experience with collective agreements and working in a unionized setting; Experience with interpreting medical/psychological documentation preferred; Or an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated understanding of the social model of disability and experience with promoting the social model within a broader organization/system. Demonstrated experience supporting learners with issues related to disability and accommodation in an educational setting, post-secondary environment preferred. Demonstrated ability to build, manage and provide leadership to cohesive teams, and implement change resulting in improvements to service quality, staff productivity and systems efficiency. Excellent written and verbal communication skills including the ability to present information to diverse audiences. Advanced ability to work collaboratively, effectively, and cross-functionally across levels within the organization. Demonstrated ability to foster positive relationships with external community partners. Demonstrated business acumen, strong work ethic, and professional integrity when representing the university. Proven expertise in developing, planning, and managing projects, with exceptional ability to prioritize tasks, self-direct, and take proactive initiative. Expert ability to analyze data and translate insights into strategic planning, budgeting, and performance monitoring. Knowledge of University systems, structures, process and decision-making structures is an asset. Demonstrated tact and discretion in preparing, disclosing and handling information of a confidential and/or sensitive nature. Ability to travel between campuses is required. Competencies Leadership: KPU employees inspire, coach, mentor, and support students, employees and KPU as a whole in achieving objectives. Accountability: KPU employees demonstrate fiscal accountability and take ownership for their actions, decisions and results. Continuous Improvement: KPU employees take a creative approach to opportunities, exploring unique ways to create optimal value for the KPU community. Collaboration: KPU employees work in functional and cross-functional teams, coming together to solve complex issues and accomplish objectives that will benefit the KPU community. Salary Information The above compensation range is the span between the minimum and maximum base salary for a position. Typically, initial salary placement is approximately halfway between the minimum and the maximum. This represents an employee that possesses full job knowledge, qualifications and experience for the position. In the normal course, employees will be hired, transferred or promoted between the minimum and approximately halfway of the salary range for a job with consideration given to internal equity. Want to know more? Click here to view the full job description. Application Process To apply for this opportunity, please submit your cover letter and resume as one document via KPU\u2019s Career Centre. Please note, the Search Committee will begin the shortlisting process on October 16, 2026 , although the position will remain open until October 30, 2026. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4747": {"title": "Divisional Program Technician, Metal Trades", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Divisional Program Technician, Metal Trades Department/Faculty Faculty of Trades & Technology Home Campus (Location) Cloverdale Tech - Surrey, BC Employment Duration Permanent Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4747 Internal Closing Date: August 7, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 11-5 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $34.75 to $38.50 per hour Employment Type: Permanent Full Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Hours of Work (BCGEU): 7:30am-3:00pm Hours per Week (BCGEU): 35 We are currently seeking a Divisional Program Technician, Metal Trades to join our Faculty of Trades & Technology team. Job Overview To provide support and assistance to students and faculty in various trade programs including; monitoring shop work, maintaining inventory, repairs of tools and equipment and prepare materials for learning. Priority consideration will be given to BCGEU employees currently impacted by layoff at the same or lower pay grade. Education and Experience A minimum of C Level Welding Ticket. Ability to operate and maintain forklift/shop vehicles and have Forklift certification. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Experience in monitoring student activity in a shop environment, ensuring the safe handling of materials, tools and equipment. Competence in the following software \u2013MS Office. MS Excel, Outlook. Extensive demonstrated experience with the safe use of machinery applicable to the trades. Demonstrated knowledge of WHMIS and WCB safe work procedures for the trades. Demonstrated working knowledge of the operation and routine maintenance of machine tools. Proven ability to organize work, multi-task and work to deadlines. Proven ability to deal effectively with others and to handle unusual or unexpected situations, including the ability to deal with hostile or upset clients. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing. Proven ability to display initiative, discretion and meet changing priorities; to tolerate ambiguity; to work on multiple tasks simultaneously; meet deadlines and make responsible decisions. Proven ability to work independently and as part of a team. Physical ability to lift and carry heavy items (23kg/50 pounds). Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4394": {"title": "Electrical Instructor", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Electrical Instructor Department/Faculty Faculty of Trades & Technology Home Campus (Location) Cloverdale Tech - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 1 (one) year on call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community 