4 and Electrical Foundation Level courses which may extend from a single day to several weeks, possibly leading to a regularized contract. More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: BC Construction Electrician Certificate of Qualification (CofQ) with Interprovincial Red Seal Endorsement (IP RSE), or a Certificate of Qualification with Interprovincial Red Seal (IP RSE) from another jurisdiction, or a BC Industrial Electrician Certificate of Qualification (CofQ) with Interprovincial Red Seal Endorsement (IP RSE), or a Certificate of Qualification with Interprovincial Red Seal (IP RSE) from another jurisdiction. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates will be required to present a demonstration lesson. Candidates will be required to undergo a Criminal Record Check. *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. This competition is for successful candidates to be added to our Qualified Faculty List. When work in this area becomes available, our faculty will draw on our Qualified Faculty List to assign work, please indicate on your application your preferred workload percentage. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4761": {"title": "Enrolment Management Coordinator, Faculty of Health", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Enrolment Management Coordinator, Faculty of Health Department/Faculty Faculty of Health Home Campus (Location) Langley, BC Employment Duration PERMANENT Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4761 Internal Closing Date: September 29, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 12 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $32.94 to $36.78 per hour Employment Type: Permanent Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Hours of Work (BCGEU): 8:30am-4:30pm Hours per Week (BCGEU): 35 We are currently seeking an Enrolment Management Coordinator, Faculty of Health to join our Faculty of Health team. Job Overview The Enrolment Management Coordinator is instrumental in shaping the leadership landscape within the recruitment and admissions cycle, and student progression in the Faculty of Health (FOH). Beyond supporting student recruitment, admissions, and retention, the coordinator assumes a leadership role in defining the overarching strategy and direction for FOH related processes. In a leadership role within the recruitment and admissions cycle, the Coordinator takes charge of devising and executing inventive strategies to draw in high-caliber students for the FOH. This extends to leading the selection process for FOH\u2019s limited intake programs that have unique application requirements; and monitoring student progression to facilitate full course sections and the re-entry of students. This leadership role includes actively shaping the strategic development of FOH procedures to ensure they align with the FOH\u2019s mission and goals. Through a comprehensive leadership approach, the Coordinator plays a pivotal role in fostering the growth and success of the Faculty of Health. Priority consideration will be given to BCGEU employees currently impacted by layoff at the same or lower pay grade. Education and Experience Diploma or completion of two years\u2019 post-secondary education. Progressive general office experience that includes three years\u2019 experience in a similar position within a unionized environment; post-secondary work experience is an asset. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated knowledge of policies and procedures related to post-secondary selective entry admissions. Experience in student recruitment, reviewing and providing feedback on application submissions, letters and interviews. Proven ability to meet changing priorities, multitasking, work to deadlines and make responsible decisions while maintaining high levels of customer service. Excellent interpersonal, organization, planning, coordination, problem-solving and follow-up skills. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Be able to independently draft correspondence and reports of a routine nature based on knowledge of established style and practices. Experience with supporting committees, demonstrated ability to create agendas, record and distribute minutes. Demonstrated skills in computer and Internet applications (e.g., Windows environment, Word, Excel, email, PebblePad and web browser). Demonstrated ability to create and maintain databases and tracking systems. Demonstrated ability to work both independently and as a member of a team. Demonstrates sound judgment in identifying issues that require escalation and knows when and to whom concerns should be raised. Demonstrated ability to anticipate issues, identify emerging needs, and take appropriate proactive steps to support students and program operations Must have access to reliable, independent transportation to travel regularly between campuses (Langley, Surrey, and Richmond). Experience handling confidential information. Possession of a valid driver\u2019s license and access to a vehicle is required. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4812": {"title": "Entertainment Arts Mentors", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Entertainment Arts Mentors Department/Faculty Faculty of Arts Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration 1 year Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4812 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: On-Call Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Dean or designate. SUMMARY The Mentor is responsible for supporting and providing feedback to students of the assigned projects as provided at the start of term. Mentors provide weekly feedback, guide students in their field of expertise. Mentors are expected to do a total of 13 weekly mentoring sessions with students and the sessions are scheduled during weekdays (generally after regular work hours), and potentially on Saturdays. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Provide students with weekly feedback on their projects Help students to scope, plan, and execute their projects Encourage and motivate students through constructive feedback Sets and models a high standard of professional behaviour and appropriate appearance Adheres to the Policies and Procedures of the universit QUALIFICATIONS Education and Experience Demonstrate familiarity and experience in one or more of the following discplines: 2D Animation 3D Animation/3D Modelling Game Development Video Production A minimum of one accredited published movie, game, or app title and/or 3 years of industry experience in an appropriate area of development Relevant degree/diploma is advantageous Experience working with and teaching students is advantageous Skills and Abilities Excellent communication, organizational, time management and interpersonal skills Critical thinking and problem-solving skills Ability to interpret and apply university, government, agency and departmental policies, procedures, and guidelines Ability to exercise a high level of initiative and responsibility Ability to use tact and discretion to deal with or settle complex requests or complaints Ability to communicate effectively with people who have limited English language proficiency SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $80.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4717": {"title": "Faculty of Arts, Journalism and Communications", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Faculty of Arts, Journalism and Communications Department/Faculty Office of the President Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 12 MONTHS Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4717 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): We are seeking a Student Assistant to support the Faculty of Arts, Journalism and Communications . The student will provide assistance in researching, interviewing, writing, and editing for the KPU 50th anniversary book project. PRINCIPAL DUTIES Fact-finding about KPU\u2019s history and various individuals involved in KPU Interviewing people involved in KPU Transcribing interviews and writing profiles of people involved in KPU Editing other students\u2019 written work Reviewing profiles with interviewees Creating and maintaining the project website and social media accounts REQUIREMENTS Strong written and verbal communication skills Must be a journalism or creative writing student Reliable and hardworking Familiarity with basic principles of web design and social media Interested in history and post-secondary education This position is reserved for KPU Students only. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4829": {"title": "Future Students' Office Student Ambassador", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Future Students' Office Student Ambassador Department/Faculty Student Services - Registrar's Office Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 6 Months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4829 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Regular travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): SUMMARY The Student Assistant will work with team members in the Future Students' Office on a variety of recruitment initiatives. He/she performs student engagement and recruitment related activities, as well as assists with events and other activities and general duties as needed. Successful Student Assistants are enthusiastic, outgoing, quick-thinking, and possess creative problem-solving skills. They are passionate about sharing their experiences at KPU with prospective students and parents. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. PRINCIPLE DUTIES Engage with prospective students through various channels (events etc.) Assist events team with planning, setup, coordination and operation logistics. Assist with communications activities to prospective students. Assist recruiters with presentations in communities from a student perspective. Assist in promoting events to current and prospective KPU students. Assist in preparing information packages/giveaway bags for campus tours Act as an ambassador for the University at external events creating a positive rapport with prospective students and community. COMMUNICATIONS DUTIES Assist with preparing mailing packages to prospects, students, and other audiences. OTHER DUTIES Assist with photocopying, and collation of materials for mail-outs and promotions. Assist with data collection, compilation, and interpretation. REQUIREMENTS Working towards a diploma or degree at KPU. Creative, energetic, outgoing and enthusiastic-seeking to make a difference. A strong social media user with a desire to contribute content and learn about processes, procedures and best practices. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to communicate clearly with others. Excellent customer service skills. Reliable, organized and detail oriented. Ability to effectively multi-task. Public speaking experience is an asset. Sensitive to diverse student needs. A second language is an asset, but not required. Problem solver, works independently and meets deadlines. Working Knowledge of Microsoft Office. Available to work evenings and weekends as needed. AVAILABILITY Work schedule will be approximately 8 - 12 hours weekly. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4852": {"title": "GAME DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTOR", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description GAME DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTOR Department/Faculty Faculty of Arts Home Campus (Location) Faculty - All Campuses Employment Duration QFL Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4852 Internal Closing Date: October 24, 2026 External Closing Date: October 24, 2026 # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Faculty Pay Scale Employment Type: Qualified Faculty List Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Faculty (Kwantlen Faculty Association) Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ENTERTAINMENT ARTS - GAME DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTOR POSITION TYPE: QFL (Qualified Faculty List) POSITION START: January 1, 2027 KPU proudly offers all learners opportunities to achieve success in a diverse range of programs that blend theory and practice, critical understanding, and social and ethical awareness necessary for good citizenship and rewarding careers. FACULTY OVERVIEW: Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is the fourth largest university in the province of British Columbia and serves communities in the South Fraser region and beyond. \u00a0A leader in innovative, interdisciplinary education with a teaching-focused mandate, KPU offers all learners opportunities to achieve the highest standards of academic performance. Our many programs of study provide applied learning and broad-based university education. Within KPU, the Faculty of Arts has over 6000 full-time students and over 300 faculty members from across the Humanities and Social Sciences. The Faculty of Arts includes 19 departments and 21 programs at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The Faculty is also home to two Canada Research Chairs: the first in Lifespan Cognition, and the second in South Asian Literary and Cultural Studies. Many of our programs offer opportunities for experiential education through practicums, co-ops, international field-schools and exchanges, service learning, community engagement, and research collaborations. For more information about the Faculty of Arts, please visit our website at: https://www.kpu.ca/arts . POSITION OVERVIEW: The Entertainment Arts program within the Faculty of Arts at Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) seeks to establish a list of faculty qualified to teach in the program and who will be eligible for future course contracts on a per-semester basis. Applications are invited from individuals with expertise related to the fields of Game Design and Development , and the areas listed below. Courses may be offered during the day or evening, online or in-person at KPU\u2019s Richmond campus, and faculty are expected to be available to teach in either delivery mode. Video Game Design experience in a senior or better role on at least two shipped titles, especially in the fields of: Level Design System Design Direct experience with technical and in-engine design tools, especially Unreal and Unity Must provide evidence of relevant design knowledge and experience Strong understanding of the intersection of various game development fields, including narrative, programming, technical design, game art, production (but not necessarily direct experience in all of these) Strong presentation and English communication skills Ability to provide verbal and written feedback to students to improve their work Comfort and experience with conflict resolution techniques For more information about Entertainment Arts course offerings, please consult the following link: https://calendar.kpu.ca/courses-az/enta/ More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: Preference will be given to individuals who have previously taught courses in a field of study listed above, who have significant professional, industry-related experience acquired within the last three years, and who have a record of teaching excellence at the post-secondary level. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates are asked to submit: A link to Demo reel on CV and Cover Letter A cover letter which clearly identifies: The field(s) of study in which you are qualified to teach The type of position in which you are interested: a one-year position at 50% or more (Non-regular, Type 2), and/or single-semester contract work of three or fewer sections (Non-regular, Type 1) A curriculum vitae with links to a portfolio site Evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., course evaluations, student survey results, peer review reports, past syllabi, or equivalent) A statement of teaching philosophy that discusses important elements of your teaching, such as: How it is informed by your professional, industry-related experience How it incorporates approaches to equity, diversity, inclusion, and decolonization The names and contact information of three referees able to comment on your teaching ability and professional, industry-related experience. Please note that incomplete applications will not be considered. *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. This competition is for successful candidates to be added to our Qualified Faculty List. When work in this area becomes available, the Qualified Faculty List will be drawn upon to assign work. As such, please indicate on your application your preferred workload percentage. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4821": {"title": "Health Science Instructor, Qualified Faculty List", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Health Science Instructor, Qualified Faculty List Department/Faculty Faculty of Science Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration Qualified Faculty List Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4821 Internal Closing Date: September 25, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 5 *Salary Information: Faculty Pay Scale Employment Type: Qualified Faculty List Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Faculty (Kwantlen Faculty Association) Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): HEALTH SCIENCE INSTRUCTOR POSITION TYPE: QUALIFIED FACULTY LIST FACULTY OVERVIEW: As Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is the fourth largest university in the province of British Columbia and serves communities in the South Fraser region and beyond. A Leader in innovative education with a teaching-focused mandate, KPU offers all learners opportunities to achieve the highest standards of academic performance. Within KPU, the Faculty of Science has over 1,500 full-time students and over 200 faculty members and instructors from across the natural and applied sciences. Faculty of Science includes nine departments and over 30 programs at the undergraduate level, with offerings at all four KPU campuses. The faculty is also home to Canada Research Chair: Dr. Cayley Velazquez and Sherman Jen Research Chair, Dr. Paul Adams. The Faculty of Science offers experiential learning through hands-on curriculum and co-ops and research collaboration opportunities with KPU\u2019s Institute for Sustainable Horticulture (ISH), Institute of Sustainable Food Systems (ISFS), and Applied Genomics Center (AGC). As well, our faculty is home to over a hectare of horticulture field lab and working farm and a state-of-the art brewery, which has been recognized internationally and locally, winning BC Brewery of the Year in 2019. For more information about the Faculty of Science, please visit our website at: kpu.ca/science POSITION OVERVIEW: Kwantlen Polytechnic University\u2019s Faculty of Science is currently seeking applications for Health Science instructors to join the Department of Biological and Health Sciences Qualified Faculty List for the Health Science Degree Program. We welcome applications from qualified instructors with research expertise or industry/sector experience in health policy, administration and leadership, allied health, business, and/or clinical research and development. Experience in the areas of health informatics, analytics, data science, and precision medicine are an asset. Courses may include Introduction to Health Science and upper-level topics such as Health Business, Health Program Planning and Evaluation, Populations and Policy, Applications to Health Science, Pharmacology, Nutrition, Health and Aging, and Critical Evaluation. Health Science is a recently developed and rapidly growing undergraduate program offered within the Department of Biological and Health Sciences at KPU. We provide an experiential learning approach in which students gain foundational knowledge in the basic sciences and practical knowledge in clinical, public, community and population health to understand current and emerging health issues and the policies, systems, and technology used to advance health and wellness. We offer a Bachelor of Science in Health Science degree, along with honours, minor, and co-op options. Successful applicants will work collaboratively with department members and colleagues across the broader KPU community to continue shaping this exciting program. More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: We seek a scholar who possesses, at minimum, a Master\u2019s degree (Ph.D. preferred) in health science, public health, public administration, human biology, or another equivalent field. The ideal candidate will have excellent written and oral communication skills as well as recent post-secondary teaching or equivalent research, scholarly, or professional experience demonstrating currency in a health science related discipline. We are looking for a scholar that is excited to develop connections to industry and/or community partners to advance course-based experiential learning opportunities. Those interested in applying can find more information on our courses by visiting our website at: https://www.kpu.ca/science/health-science APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates are asked to submit: Statement of teaching philosophy (maximum one page) Description of how you will incorporate your research, professional experience and/or network to support undergraduate teaching (maximum one page) Current curriculum vitae that includes information about previous courses taught and/or relevant research, scholarly, or professional experience\\ Names of three referees willing to comment on your ability to contribute to a degree-granting Biological and Health Sciences department. Please forward your application package with cover letter. *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. This competition is for successful candidates to be added to our Qualified Faculty List. When work in this area becomes available, the Qualified Faculty List will be drawn upon to assign work. As such, please indicate on your application if you are interested in being added to this list and your preferred workload percentage. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4706": {"title": "Indigenous Designer-in-Residence", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Indigenous Designer-in-Residence Department/Faculty Wilson School of Design Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration Please see details below Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4706 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Director, Strategy and Business Development, Wilson School of Design. SUMMARY The Wilson School of Design (WSD) invites applications from established or emerging Indigenous designers, including First Nations, M\u00e9tis, and Inuit of Canada, for a position as Indigenous Designer-in-Residence. This residency will support Indigenous designers in the research and creation of new works, and is open to designers in a variety of fields, including but not restricted to fashion and apparel design, graphic design, interior design, product design, and other interdisciplinary design practices. The Indigenous Designer-in-Residence will be able to divide their time between their own creative practice and contributing to the Wilson School of Design. In their application, candidates are encouraged to detail how they envision engaging with the Wilson School of Design and the broader KPU community of faculty, students, and staff. For more information about the Wilson School of Design, please visit our website at https://www.kpu.ca/design. An applicant does not need to have to an expertise in all disciplines, but have at least one expertise and a common fundamental understanding of others. Designers will be compensated for the duration of their residency. There will also be funding available for KPU/WSD-specific events, expenses for materials and supplies, as well as for honoraria for designers whom the Indigenous Designer-in-Residence may want to invite to events. Applications should include: A curriculum vitae or resume A cover letter or video that includes your statement of interest; a proposal of the design project you will undertake during the residency; and a description of the kinds of events you would like to plan, and how you see these contributing to the KPU/WSD community. (For video submissions, please provide a link to a website or Google doc.) Please include a statement clearly indicating your availability to be present on KPU campuses (primarily the Richmond campus). A letter of support or documentation regarding your connections to Indigenous community and/or an Indigenous organization, as well as lived experience. A portfolio: up to 10 original works with titles and dates. Please provide the portfolio through a link to a website; or links to videos or audio files; or a link to a Google doc. The names of two references: One from community and one professional. KPU is committed to the Truth and Reconciliation Commission (TRC) Calls to Action and to supporting Indigenous designers and their representation and visibility within KPU and its broader communities. This program will foster community engagement and will have a positive impact on both the designers and the KPU community through sharing, dialogue, creativity, and intercultural communication. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES The organization and hosting of a series of events for the WSD and KPU that may include the following: designer talks/critiques; workshops; studio visits; outreach activities Giving guest lectures, or workshops within the WSD and KPU. Consulting with students and designers of various abilities. Participating in events organized by the WSD and/or KPU Meeting regularly with the Director, Strategy and Business Development, WSD QUALIFICATIONS Relevant community-based and/or professional experience rooted in Indigenous communities, knowledges, and traditions Designers should be active in their design discipline(s) with an established or emerging record of work as made evident through websites, exhibitions, showcases, reviews, articles, etc. A record of participation in the design community and related events Enthusiasm for connecting with KPU\u2019s community members from a variety of areas and disciplines Willingness to organize and plan events in collaboration with the WSD Communications and Events Coordinator. SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly rate: $45.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4782": {"title": "Indigenous Services Student Assistant", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Indigenous Services Student Assistant Department/Faculty Student Services - Indigenous Services for Students Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 4 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4782 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): SUMMARY: Reporting to the Coordinator, Indigenous Student Transition and Engagement, the Student Assistant acts as a peer liaison and host to Indigenous students through one-on-one or small group interactions focusing on creating a safe and welcoming environment and promoting student engagement. The student assistant (also referred to as a Gathering Place Host) also supports a variety of cultural, social, and educational events at KPU. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. PRINCIPAL DUTIES: Act as a peer liaison to assist students by identifying various KPU student support services and/or make referrals to appropriate departments and/or community organizations Greet and welcome students and guests to the Gathering Place (GP) in a warm and friendly manner Promote student life activities and events Contribute to peer-run bi-monthly email newsletter and social media that highlight scholarship and funding opportunities, campus and community events Support team event planning for Indigenous cultural and community events Assist Coordinator at educational and community events, as needed Monitor GP resources and maintain bulletin board so that it is relevant and organized Assist students in the GP with computers and supplies, as needed Attend weekly departmental team meetings REQUIREMENTS: Applicant must be of Indigenous (First Nations, M\u00e9tis, or Inuit) ancestry Must be enrolled at KPU as a full time student and in good academic standing Must be familiar with available student support services and campus resources Must have excellent interpersonal skills Must have experience in MS office; and knowledge of online platforms such as Moodle would be considered an asset Ability to multi-task Must be willing to travel to other campus, as needed SALARY INFORMATION: Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4809": {"title": "Institute for Sustainable Horticulture Research Assistant Pool", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Institute for Sustainable Horticulture Research Assistant Pool Department/Faculty Institute for Sustainable Horticulture Home Campus (Location) Langley, BC Employment Duration On-Call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4809 Internal Closing Date: December 18, 2026 External Closing Date: December 18, 2026 # of Openings: 5 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE Research Assistants report to The Director, and various project leaders involved in research with the Institute for Sustainable Horticulture. SUMMARY The Institute for Sustainable Horticulture partners with agricultural and agri-technology companies in our region to support innovation with research and development projects that promote sustainability in the sector. Current projects include developing microbial biocontrol products for pests and diseases, natural soil amendments and inoculants, biofertilizers, agritech applications, alternate growing systems, and soil microbial health. Work hours and start dates are dependent on external research grants and can be either part-time or full-time. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Greenhouse and growth chamber plant trials with biostimulants, biocontrols Laboratory trials with beneficial microbes involving sterile technique, monitoring growth and interactions Maintaining greenhouse crops, transplanting, pruning, harvesting, IPM scouting, releasing bios, cleaning pots, and general greenhouse support Soil sample collecting and processing Support field trials off site Collect, record and analyze data, assist with data interpretation and contemplate what, why and how Other duties as assigned QUALIFICATIONS These positions are suitable for students and new graduates with interest in biocontrol and horticulture, e.g. Horticulture Diploma, Plant Health Degree. The work requires a strong attention to detail and the ability to stay focused when performing repeated tasks. Some positions require travel between KPU and field sites. SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $21.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4502": {"title": "Lab Instructor, Faculty of Arts", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Lab Instructor, Faculty of Arts Department/Faculty Faculty of Arts Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration On-Call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4502 Internal Closing Date: March 7, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: 13 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $33.88 to $37.81 per hour Employment Type: On-Call Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday Hours of Work (BCGEU): On-Call Hours per Week (BCGEU): On-Call We are currently seeking a Lab Instructor to join the Faculty of Arts Job Overview This position reports to the Divisional Business Manager and works in collaboration with the Department Chair/Coordinator, instructors, and a team of Lab Instructors. The Lab Instructor assists the Faculty of Arts with overall course delivery in designated departments by assuming responsibility for reviewing material with students, student guidance and assessment (including participation in the class and lab component of any course). In addition to instructing students on lab procedures and the use of lab equipment, the Lab Instructor researches, conduct experiments, and introduces new materials, equipment and procedures to advance the program. The Lab Instructor may support any program or course offered by the relevant department(s). The class and lab assignments and learning objectives will be provided by the instructor. \u00a0Standard and prescribed industry practices will be created in collaboration between instructors, Lab Instructors, and students. \u00a0Using these, Lab Instructors are expected to perform their duties with a minimum of managerial supervision and work effectively with other Lab Instructors, faculty members, student mentors, the KPU community, and the Entertainment Arts industry. Education and Experience Graduation from a 2-year Entertainment Arts program within the past five years is required. Experience tutoring and working with students is an asset Proven junior industry-level proficiency regarding current technology and software used in the Entertainment Arts program(s) Priority will be given to candidates with experience in the specialty area of rigging. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Experience working collaboratively as an effective team player. Proven ability to take initiative when working both independently and as part of a team. Proven ability to juggle and prioritize tasks, work to meet deadlines and demands, make responsible decisions, and determine when to seek advice. Experience developing, planning, and administering systems and/or projects. Demonstrated attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment in making critical decisions. Experience in identifying problems, evaluating alternatives, consulting with stakeholders, and implementing effective solutions. Proven ability to think innovatively and creatively to implement new systems and procedures. \u00a0Evaluate their effectiveness. Experience in Microsoft Office suite (e.g. Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint, Word). Proven ability to quickly learn new software and equipment as needed. Proven ability to exercise tact, diplomacy, and resolve conflicts. Experience to providing guidance, training, and instruction to others. Demonstrated innovation and change-management skills which include supporting and encouraging new ideas and approaches to build organizational efficiency. Excellent communication, organizational, time management, and interpersonal skills is required. Demonstrated ability to maintain discretion and confidentiality is required. Please click here for a more detailed job description As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4755": {"title": "Laboratory Instructor, Biology", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Laboratory Instructor, Biology Department/Faculty Faculty of Science Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration On-Call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4755 Internal Closing Date: August 24, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 5 *Salary Information: 13 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $33.88 to $37.81 per hour Employment Type: On-Call Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Flex Hours Required Hours of Work (BCGEU): On-Call (varies) Hours per Week (BCGEU): On-Call (varies) We are currently seeking a Laboratory Instructor, Biology to join our Faculty of Science team. Job Overview The Laboratory Instructor - Biology participates in the Biology Department with the overall course delivery by assuming responsibility for instruction, student guidance and assessment within a lab environment. The Laboratory Instructor - Biology may be assigned to work alongside other Laboratory Instructors (or a faculty member) or alone in fulfilling the above functions. They are expected to perform with a minimum of managerial supervision by the Lab Supervisor and Dean\u2019s Office. Lab responsibilities may involve any university level (first to fourth year) or applied program service courses offered in the Biology Department\u2019s educational plan. Special Considerations: The Biology faculty is ultimately responsible for course delivery and development, including the laboratory portion of any course. The Laboratory Instructor - Biology assists the faculty through their role in the labs in achieving this aim. \u00a0The Lab Instructor \u2013 Biology and faculty work collegially to meet a common aim. Workload and scheduled contact hours can be found in the \u201cWORKLOAD GUIDELINES FOR FACULTY OF SCIENCE LAB INSTRUCTORS\u201d. The Laboratory Instructor - Biology works in compliance with current WHMIS regulations and directs students in all aspects of lab safety. They must have read the Laboratory Safety and Biosafety Manuals, completed Biosafety and Fire Safety Training and be aware of their potential role and responsibilities in the event of a chemical or biohazardous spill or accident. They must comply with all Biosafety and Biosecurity requirements of the Canadian biosafety standard of the Public Health Agency of Canada while working with Containment Level 2 organisms as it pertains to the department\u2019s pathogens and toxins license. Education and Experience Baccalaureate degree, Masters preferred, in Biology. Proven related teaching experience is an asset. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated good working knowledge of the course content and competence in laboratory techniques pertaining to the instruction of any year biology courses. Demonstrated good working knowledge of the course content and competence in laboratory techniques pertaining to one or more of the following \u2013 introduction to biology, cell biology, microbiology, genetics, ecology, botany, marine biology, zoology, anatomy and physiology and human anatomy and physiology. Demonstrated working knowledge of the operation and routine maintenance of laboratory equipment and apparatus. Proven ability to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing. Demonstrated ability to provide instruction to undergraduate students in a laboratory setting. Demonstrated working knowledge of current WHMIS, biosafety and other preventative measures required for the safe \u00a0 operation of the biology lab. Proven ability to establish and maintain effective relationships with people of varied background and experience. Proven ability to work in a team-oriented environment. Ability to travel between campuses. Please Note: When applying to this staffing process, you are not applying for a specific job, but to an inventory (or pool) for future on-call vacancies. As vacancies become available, applicants who meet the qualifications will be contacted and may require further assessment depending on the requirements of the assignment. Individuals should have a flexible schedule with the ability to work at any of our five campuses. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4826": {"title": "Laboratory Instructor - Physics", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Laboratory Instructor - Physics Department/Faculty Faculty of Science Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration PERMANENT Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4826 Internal Closing Date: October 9, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 13 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $33.88 to $37.81 per hour Employment Type: Permanent Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Regular travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Flex Hours Required Hours of Work (BCGEU): 8-9am to 4-5pm Hours per Week (BCGEU): 21 We are currently seeking a Laboratory Instructor - Physics to join our Faculty of Science team. Job Overview The Laboratory Instructor - Physics assists faulty with the overall course delivery by assuming responsibility for instruction, student guidance and assessment (including report marking in the lab component of any course). The Laboratory Instructor - Physics may be assigned to work alongside other Laboratory Instructors (or a faculty member) or alone in fulfilling the above functions. The incumbent is expected to perform with a minimum of managerial supervision by the Dean. Lab responsibilities may involve any preparatory, first and second year university level or applied program service courses offered in the Physics Department\u2019s educational plan. Priority consideration will be given to BCGEU employees currently impacted by layoff at the same or lower pay grade. Education and Experience Have a B.Sc. in physics, or its equivalent, supplemented by previous related laboratory experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Have a good working knowledge of the course content, laboratory equipment and techniques pertaining to the instruction of physics courses at the preparatory, first and second year level. Have a working knowledge of the operation and routine maintenance of laboratory equipment and apparatus. Be able to communicate effectively in speech and writing the facts, figures and explanations and procedures in a laboratory setting. Be able to effectively demonstrate proper laboratory techniques. Be able to use standard word processing and spreadsheet programs on Windows-based and/or Macintosh personal computers. Be able to perform general maintenance and troubleshooting of computers. Be able to establish and maintain effective relationships with people of varied backgrounds and experience. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4834": {"title": "Marketing Student Assistant (Creative Studio)", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Marketing Student Assistant (Creative Studio) Department/Faculty Marketing Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 6 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4834 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): Are you a current KPU student interested in contributing to KPU's branded gifts and swag? We are looking for students in design or other creative journeys who are interested in working with our Marketing Services team for short periods of time to assist in designing branded KPU merchandise such as clothing and other items. ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This position reports to the Manager, Brand and Marketing Operations within the Marketing department. SUMMARY The Marketing Student Assistant (Creative Studio) supports the development of creative products and branded experiences that celebrate and promote Kwantlen Polytechnic University while providing meaningful work-integrated learning opportunities. Working collaboratively with the Marketing department and, where appropriate, faculty members and technical staff across the University, the Student Assistant will contribute creative ideas, concepts, prototypes and finished products that represent KPU's brand and enhance the student experience. Projects will be tailored to the successful candidate's area of study, creative strengths and available hours. Depending on the student's discipline, projects may include product design, apparel, illustration, ceramics, woodworking, textiles, digital fabrication, packaging, print design, photography, visual art, or other creative works that support the University's marketing initiatives. This position provides students with the opportunity to apply classroom learning in a professional environment while building a portfolio of real-world work that may ultimately be produced, displayed or distributed by KPU. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Collaborate with the Marketing department to develop creative concepts, products and experiences that support the KPU brand. Design, prototype and refine unique products and merchandise for use in student recruitment, events, alumni engagement, donor recognition and other University initiatives. Participate in brainstorming sessions and contribute innovative ideas that showcase the creativity and diversity of the KPU community. Work with faculty members, instructors and technical staff to utilize specialized equipment, studios and fabrication spaces where appropriate. Prepare concepts, prototypes and production-ready files for review and approval. Incorporate feedback throughout the creative process while maintaining project timelines and quality standards. Research emerging trends in product design, sustainability, university merchandise and creative experiences. Assist in documenting creative projects for marketing, promotional and portfolio purposes. Support the presentation or showcasing of completed work through University events, retail opportunities and other marketing initiatives. Represent KPU professionally while collaborating with students, faculty and staff across multiple disciplines. QUALIFICATIONS Currently enrolled in a diploma, degree or trades program at KPU. Demonstrated creativity through coursework, portfolio, personal projects or previous experience. Interest in design, product development, fabrication, creative technologies, fine arts, trades or other creative disciplines. Strong creative thinking and problem-solving skills. Ability to receive and apply constructive feedback throughout an iterative design process. Strong organizational and time management skills with the ability to balance multiple priorities. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as part of a collaborative team. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Reliable, self-motivated and detail oriented. Experience with creative software, tools, equipment or production methods relevant to the student's discipline is considered an asset. WORK-INTEGRATED LEARNING This position is designed to provide students with meaningful hands-on experience by contributing to real marketing initiatives while developing professional skills and industry-ready portfolio pieces. Students will gain experience collaborating with stakeholders, managing creative projects, presenting concepts, responding to feedback and developing products that have the potential to become part of KPU's brand and campus experience. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4574": {"title": "NR1 Horticulture Instructor: Landscape Machinery", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description NR1 Horticulture Instructor: Landscape Machinery Department/Faculty Faculty of Science Home Campus (Location) Langley, BC Employment Duration 4 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4574 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Faculty Pay Scale Employment Type: Faculty Contract Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Faculty (Kwantlen Faculty Association) Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): CONTRACT INSTRUCTOR POSITION TYPE : NR1 POSITION START: September 2026 FACULTY OVERVIEW: As Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is the fourth largest university in the province of British Columbia and serves communities in the South Fraser region and beyond. A Leader in innovative education with a teaching-focused mandate, KPU offers all learners opportunities to achieve the highest standards of academic performance. Within KPU, the Faculty of Science has over 1,500 full-time students and over 200 faculty members and instructors from across the natural and applied sciences. Faculty of Science includes nine departments and over 30 programs at the undergraduate level, with offerings at all four KPU campuses. The faculty is also home to Canada Research Chair: Dr. Paul Adams. The Faculty of Science offers experiential learning through hands-on curriculum and co-ops and research collaboration opportunities with KPU\u2019s Institute for Sustainable Horticulture (ISH), Institute of Sustainable Food Systems (ISFS), and Applied Genomics Center (AGC). As well, our faculty is home to over a hectare of horticulture field lab and working farm and a state-of-the art brewery, which has been recognized internationally and locally, winning BC Brewery of the Year in 2019. For more information about the Faculty of Science, please visit our https://www.kpu.ca/science . POSITION OVERVIEW: The School of Horticulture invites applications for Part-Time Non-Regular Type 1 Contract Instructor(s) to teach HORT 1118 Basic Machinery Operation and Maintenance and HORT 2432 Grounds Machinery Maintenance , at the KPU Langley campus. HORT 1118 is offered in the Fall and Spring semesters with additional classes added depending on demand. HORT 2432 is offered based on demand. Additional courses may include: AHHA 1001 Equipment and Safety and AHHA 1026 Machinery and Equipment. The following is a brief description of the specific courses and supplementary qualifications: HORT 1118 Basic Machinery Operation and Maintenance Students will be introduced to horticulture machinery. They will perform preventative maintenance. Students will safely demonstrate machinery operations. Students will complete a Workplace Hazardous Materials Information System (WHMIS) Certificate. Course Learning Outcomes: Describe the function and working principles of horticulture machinery Perform machinery operation and preventative maintenance Use appropriate safety systems and apparel Use basic hand tools in machinery preventative maintenance Describe machinery storage procedures Evaluate machinery specifications for specific horticultural tasks Recognize alternative power sources Apply the Workers' Compensation Act in the workplace Recognize environmental issues caused by horticulture machinery Complete a WHMIS Certificate HORT 2432 Grounds Machinery Maintenance Students will perform maintenance on turfgrass machinery used on a golf course or in parks facilities. They will repair and maintain machinery used for turf cultivation, renovation, mowing, spraying, and other types of grounds maintenance. Students will design a layout plan for a mechanics shop and storage facility following environmental and safety guidelines. AHHA 1001 Equipment and Safety A Landscape Horticulturist has a working knowledge of a variety of equipment and safety related functions. They will use motorized equipment and personal protective equipment and safety related equipment. Apprentices will demonstrate proper selection and use of personal protection equipment. They will describe the procedure for using a fire extinguisher and identify jurisdictional regulations, including WHMIS and WBC Regulations. Apprentices will identify basic engine types, and be able to perform pre-start inspections, and perform equipment maintenance and repairs. AHHA 1026 Machinery and Equipment A Landscape Horticulturist has a working knowledge of a variety of equipment and safety related functions. They will use motorized equipment and personal protective equipment and safety related equipment. Apprentices will demonstrate power tool maintenance and storage. They will identify basic vehicle systems and components. They will inspect vehicles and equipment and operate motorized vehicles. Applicants interested in applying to teach can find further information on the School of Horticulture by visiting our website at https://www.kpu.ca/hort . More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum qualifications for this position include at least five years of relevant industry experience in the use and maintenance of landscape and turf equipment and machinery. Preference will be given to candidates who hold a Landscape Horticulturist Red Seal, another recognized industry certification, and an appropriate bachelor\u2019s degree. Teaching experience is considered an asset. The successful candidate will be expected to organize field trips that provide students with opportunities to observe and learn from professionally maintained sites. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates are asked to submit: Current resume CV Cover letter highlighting key qualifications and teaching approach Please combine required documents into one single file to upload. *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. When possible, priority will be given to the candidate(s) who can maximize the FTE either individually, or collectively, as such please indicate on your application your preferred workload percentage. This competition could also be used to add candidates to our Qualified Faculty List, therefore also please indicate on your application if you are interested in being added to this list. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4818": {"title": "Photographer/Videographer", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Photographer/Videographer Department/Faculty Marketing Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 6 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4818 Internal Closing Date: September 16, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to the Manager, Branding and Marketing Operations. SUMMARY On a freelance basis, the successful candidate will shoot and execute photo and video services for Marketing Services at Kwantlen Polytechnic University. The successful candidate will report to the Manager, Branding and Marketing Operations and work closely with leadership, other members of the Marketing team, in addition to colleagues from across KPU to create engaging multimedia content that captures, informs and engages audiences. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Create engaging internal and external visuals and video content using KPU\u2019s established brand guidelines and visual elements Work with team members on photo/video shoot pre-planning, storyboarding, and creative ideation, establishing a clear understanding of the storyline and purpose of the video's creation, and its desired look and feel Serve as a camera operator on photo/video shoots and events as required Edit photos in a timely manner and share internally and externally as required Operate computer editing software and equipment used for video media, effects and motion graphics Edit videos to include preselected music, interviews, sound clips and other important aspects of the project Ensure the correct formatting and presentation for finalized videos according to specifications QUALIFICATIONS Minimum two (2) years of direct photo and video experience. A creative, collaborative team-player with a passion for visual storytelling Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, and receptive to feedback Proficient experience with editing software (After Effects, Premiere, Photoshop, Illustrator, etc.) Solid understanding of how to optimize video content for all social platforms Access to your own equipment (University to provide laptop and editing software) Duties will require the ability to travel to all 5 KPU campuses (Surrey, Langley, Cloverdale, and Richmond) and other locations in the Lower Mainland. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS Portfolio Submission: Please provide a link to a portfolio or include samples of your recent work (video and photography). SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $32.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4711": {"title": "President and Vice Chancellor", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description President and Vice Chancellor Department/Faculty Office of the President Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration PERMANENT Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4711 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: President Salary Level - $250,000 to $282,500 Employment Type: Permanent Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Administration/Management Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): The President & Vice Chancellor (\u201cPresident\u201d), serving as the CEO, is responsible for the leadership and general management of the affairs of KPU in accordance with provincial legislation and policies, and strategy set by the Board. The President articulates a direction that is congruent with the KPU\u2019s mission, vision, values, and goals in furthering its academic standards and fulfilling its role as a polytechnic university in the community. The President provides strategic, visionary, informed, and effective leadership and decision-making in a complex, multi-faceted, and public context. The President ensures materials are available for Board activities and participates in the essential functions of the Board, including governance, compliance, and policy formulation. KPU is at a critical stage in its evolution; coming on the heels of a decade of growth and change, KPU\u2019s next President will lead an institution which has leveraged the considerable talents of its communities to innovate, raise its profile, rebuild its infrastructure, and solidify its partnerships, but must also work through the pressures connected with declining international student enrolment. KPU must remain agile, at the vanguard of change, with a President who understands how education will prepare tomorrow\u2019s workforce and global citizens. This is an outstanding opportunity for a dynamic leader to take KPU to the next level. Balancing the responsibilities of external relationships and internal stewardship, the President should be accessible and transparent, and able to find the common purpose amongst the institution\u2019s many communities. With an increased focus on reconciliation and decolonization; anti-racism; justice, equity, diversity, and inclusion; and environmental sustainability, the President will know how to put these ideas into meaningful action in order to create an institution that welcomes and supports all learners. Click here to read further details about this career opportunity. To Apply: KPU has partnered with Leaders International, one of Canada\u2019s leading executive search firms, on this exciting opportunity! Please email a cover letter & resume (PDF or Word Document only) to Vancouver@leadersinternational.com and indicate the role title in the subject line. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4830": {"title": "Pride Peer Leader", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Pride Peer Leader Department/Faculty Office of the Vice President, Equity & Inclusive Communities Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration March 31st, 2027 Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4830 Internal Closing Date: October 19, 2026 External Closing Date: October 19, 2026 # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to the Specialist, Gender and Sexual Equity, in the Office of Equity and Inclusive Communities. SUMMARY The Pride Peers is a peer to peer program with a specialized focus on supporting 2SLGBTQIA+ students and providing them with a safe and confidential space at KPU. The Pride Peers do not provide counselling, but they do provide confidential support, listening, and resource referral to resources. The Peer Pride Program\u2019s main objectives are to: Offer social support and mentorship to 2SLGBTQIA+KPU students Provide students with Internal and external resource navigation and referrals Advocate for enhanced student equity, diversity, inclusion and social justice at KPU This position is reserved for KPU Students only. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Be available to support students at scheduled times at Pride spaces on KPU campuses. Assist the Office of Equity and Inclusive Communities team in the development, administration and evaluation of the Pride Peers Program. This includes creating resources, facilitating activities, discussion groups, workshops and events. Provide social support and referrals to KPU students by being knowledgeable in the services and resources offered by KPU and appropriate external resources. Attend and participate in team meetings, training sessions and ongoing PD opportunities. Promote the program and represent the Pride Peers by participating in on campus outreach. With support and guidance from the Office of Equity and Inclusive Communities, promote awareness and education around sexual and gender diversity issues. Attend mandatory training sessions and team meetings. Present to groups of up to 30 participants. Will be required to work up to 15 hours per week with a flexible schedule. Occasional travel will be required between campuses and to off-campus activities/events (including on weekends). QUALIFICATIONS Successful completion of at least one (1) year at a post-secondary institution or one (1) semester at KPU Must be a current KPU Student in good academic standing https://www.kpu.ca/advising/academic-standing Must self-identify as part of the 2SLGBTQIA+ community Students with past experience in 2SLGBTQIA+ advocacy work and knowledge of 2SLGBTQIA+ issues preferred Demonstrated knowledge of resources on campus. Must have an interest in promoting awareness, education and safe spaces Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills Demonstrated leadership skills Ability to understand and maintain confidentiality and privacy Proficient in MS Office applications (Outlook, Word, PowerPoint, Excel); experience with MS Publisher or Adobe Creative Suite an asset Creative problem solving and critical thinking skills Ability to work efficiently and complete tasks independently and as part of a team Experience with event planning is an asset Salary Information Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4790": {"title": "Research Assistant, Office of Equity and Inclusive Communities", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Research Assistant, Office of Equity and Inclusive Communities Department/Faculty Office of the Vice President, Equity & Inclusive Communities Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration March, 2027 Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4790 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 5 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This position reports to Dr. Asma Sayed, Canada Research Chair in South Asian Literary and Cultural Studies. SUMMARY This is a part-time position for a Research Assistant to work with and report to Canada Research Chair, Dr. Asma Sayed, on a number of research and writing projects based on South Asian literature and cinema. This position requires occasionally working in-person with the supervisor from KPU's Surrey campus. A major or minor in English, Creative Writing, Asian Studies, Film Studies, Social Justice will be given preference. Knowledge of South Asian languages such as Hindi, Gujarati, Punjabi, Urdu, etc. is an asset. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Assisting with organizing conferences, workshops, and symposiums Collaborating with the Research Associate and supporting them Researching/Locating, collating, and annotating key literature Research, editing and typing of academic journal articles and books Develop and maintain files on issues related to the current project Conduct library and online research as required Assist with photocopying, typing, filing, and overall organization of materials Communication with faculty, peers, relevant internal and external partners as directed Prepare summary reports Supporting with writing, citations, and document layout Co-authoring short pieces (author profiles, book reviews) with the supervisor Creating infographics of key findings Support with revising, editing, and analyzing written pieces Amplifying research findings and other relevant details through social media QUALIFICATIONS Qualified candidates will have an interest in and/or knowledge of South Asian literature and cinema, and social justice issues Strong writing and communication skills Completing tasks within assigned deadlines Regular and consistent delivery of assigned tasks Experience with researching, writing, editing Ability to follow direction with minimal supervision Demonstrated strong attention to detail Ability to use MS Office tools including databases for tracking or qualitative and/or quantitative studies Good interpersonal, organization, research skills A professional and positive attitude APPLICATION PROCESS A complete application includes: A resume A statement of interest (300-500 words) that explains why you would like to work on this project A writing sample Please combine the required documents into one single document when submitting your application. *SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $22.00 - $27.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4595": {"title": "Student Ambassador, Student Affairs", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Student Ambassador, Student Affairs Department/Faculty Student Services - Student Affairs Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 4 Months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4595 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to the Communications and Events Coordinator, Student Services. SUMMARY The Student Ambassador is an integral part of Student Services and enhances the KPU student experience with prospective and current students and community members. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Engage with students and campus visitors for wayfinding and referral to services. Provide knowledgeable, timely, and professional customer service. Develop and maintain detailed records of engagements. Assist with content for divisional social media accounts. Assist with event planning, setup, coordination, and logistics. Assist with drafting and reviewing communication and marketing materials. QUALIFICATIONS Good academic standing. Good organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Experience in communications, marketing, and/or a related field is an asset. Proficient in MS Office applications. Familiar with common social media platforms. Reliable, responsible, and professional with a customer-service mindset. Able to work independently and as part of a team. Able to effectively multi-task. Sensitive to the needs of a diverse student population. Available to work across all KPU campuses as needed. Available to work evenings and weekends as needed. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4844": {"title": "Sustainability Data & Communications Support", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Sustainability Data & Communications Support Department/Faculty Office of the VP, Administration Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 7 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4844 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to the Director of Planning, Development, and Sustainability. SUMMARY The Sustainability Data & Communications Support position will assist the Office of Sustainability in advancing campus sustainability initiatives through data management, digital communications, and on-campus engagement. The successful candidate will assist with maintaining and updating energy and sustainability performance dashboards, support website content updates, and contribute to sustainability reporting and on-campus engagements. This position provides an opportunity for students to gain hands-on experience in sustainability data analysis and sustainability communications and is ideal for a student interested in combining sustainability, data analytics, community engagement, and communications to help advance institutional sustainability goals. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Dashboard and Data Support Assists in updating and maintaining energy, greenhouse gas (GHG), utility, and sustainability performance dashboards. Compiles, organizes, and validates sustainability-related data from various institutional sources. Helps develop new dashboard features and visualizations to improve data accessibility and key party understanding. Website and Communications Support Updates sustainability website content, ensuring information remains accurate, current, and accessible. Gathers, coordinates, and maintains internal and external communications content for KPU's sustainability communication channels. Helps improve the organization and presentation of sustainability information across digital platforms. Sustainability Program Support Supports outreach activities, campaigns, and events promoting sustainability on campus. Provides general administrative support to sustainability projects as needed. QUALIFICATIONS Current KPU student in good academic standing, with a minimum 2.5 GPA Knowledge of sustainability concepts, greenhouse gas accounting, or energy management. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple tasks and work independently. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4827": {"title": "System Support Technologist - Help Desk", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description System Support Technologist - Help Desk Department/Faculty IT Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 4 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4827 Internal Closing Date: October 11, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 12 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $32.94 to $36.78 per hour Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Hours of Work (BCGEU): 9:00am - 5:00pm Hours per Week (BCGEU): 35 We are currently seeking a Systems Support Technologist - Help Desk to join our Information Technology (IT) team. Job Overview To provide computer support services to students and employee users of Kwantlen University College systems. Education and Experience Completion of a Computer Systems Technology diploma or equivalent. Minimum of 2 years' experience working on a computer support service desk using remote control and basic monitoring systems. Minimum of 2 years' experience in identifying, analyzing, diagnosing and resolving complex problems over the phone. Minimum of 2 years' experience in using a technology service management system in an ITIL environment. Proven ability to work in a customer focused computer support service center. 3 years' experience in providing on-site computer desktop and peripheral support including printers, data projectors, laptops, tablets and smart phones. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Proven superior customer service skills. Working knowledge of Exchange, Active Directory and SharePoint. Thorough knowledge of ITIL incident and request management. Thorough knowledge of Microsoft Windows operating systems. Thorough knowledge of standard desktop applications (including word processing, spreadsheet, communications, databases and desktop video conferencing). Proven ability to quickly grasp new concepts and learn new systems. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing. Proven ability to deal effectively with others and to handle unusual or unexpected situations. Proven ability to work under minimal supervision, under own initiative and as an effective team member. Proven ability to independently organize work to achieve predetermined goals and meet deadlines. Possession of a valid driver\u2019s license and access to a vehicle is required. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4825": {"title": "Vice President, Human Resources", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Vice President, Human Resources Department/Faculty Human Resources Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration PERMANENT Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4825 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 18 \u2013 Administrative Salary Grid - $166,197 to $254,836 Employment Type: Permanent Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Frequent travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Administration/Management Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): The Opportunity This is a pivotal moment to join Kwantlen Polytechnic University\u2019s executive leadership team. We are seeking an experienced and visionary Vice President, Human Resources (VP HR) to guide KPU through a period of significant change and renewal. Reporting directly to the President and Vice Chancellor, the VP Human Resources is a trusted advisor and key member of the executive team \u2014 shaping the future of KPU\u2019s workforce, advancing organizational strategy, and fostering a strong, inclusive workplace culture. The VP Human Resources provides executive leadership across various positions \u2013 Director, HR Systems & Talent Development; the Director, Labour Relations; and the Director, Workforce Advisory & Compensation, as well as the Manager, Campus Security Operations and the Manager, Emergency Planning. This role is both strategic and hands-on, offering the opportunity to influence KPU\u2019s people strategy and support student success, community engagement, and institutional priorities. As VP Human Resources, you will: Serve as a trusted advisor to the President, Board, and senior leadership, guiding people strategies that align with KPU\u2019s mission and long-term priorities. Champion the employee experience, shaping programs and practices that strengthen engagement, learning, well-being, and a sense of belonging across KPU. Lead transformation by modernizing HR practices, introducing innovative approaches, and helping the university evolve through times of change. Provide strategic and operational leadership across all HR functions \u2014 including labour relations, recruitment, retention, compensation, organizational development, and employee experience. Working collaboratively with the Office of General Counsel and other institutional partners to identify and manage legal and organizational risk. Provide strategic leadership in complex employment, Human Rights, workplace investigations, regulatory, and labour relations matters, including collective bargaining, grievances, conflict resolution, and building strong, collaborative union relationships. Provide oversight and direction for Risk and Campus Safety & Security, ensuring a safe and supportive environment for students, faculty, and staff. Foster equity, diversity, inclusion, and reconciliation in all aspects of HR strategy and institutional culture. Build strong relationships with faculty, staff, and unions, fostering collaboration, trust, and effective resolution of complex issues in a unionized environment. Oversee, support and mentor a diverse HR leadership team, in order to achieve departmental and institutional goals. Strengthen connections with the communities KPU serves and collaborate with peer post-secondary institutions across BC and Canada to share expertise and advance best practices. Influence institution-wide priorities as part of KPU\u2019s executive leadership team, contributing to a student-focused, community-driven, and inclusive university. What You Bring You are a seasoned HR executive who thrives in complex environments and sees opportunity in times of change. You bring both strategic foresight and operational expertise, with a track record of leading transformation, building strong teams, and fostering inclusive workplaces in a complex unionized environment. You are trusted for your integrity, sound judgment, and ability to inspire confidence at every level of an organization. We\u2019re looking for someone who: Holds a graduate degree in a relevant discipline and has at least 10 years of senior HR leadership experience, ideally in the public sector or post-secondary. Has a proven ability to lead change, modernize practices, and guide teams through transition. Is confident advising Presidents, Boards, and senior leaders on sensitive HR and organizational matters. Builds credibility through integrity, consistency, transparency, and fairness. Demonstrates strong emotional intelligence: listens, engages, and fosters a respectful, inclusive work environment. Is deeply committed to advancing equity, diversity, inclusion, and reconciliation, and to creating a workplace where all employees feel valued and supported. Brings extensive labour relations experience, including collective bargaining, grievances, and arbitration. Has experience developing and empowering high-performing teams, balancing accountability with collaboration and service excellence. Brings resilience, adaptability, and the ability to make sound decisions in a complex, unionized environment. Want to know more? For more detailed information on this position, click here . The Location KPU is a multi-campus institution. The Human Resources offices are located at the Langley campus; however, this position will be based primarily at the Surrey Main campus. Application Process To apply for this opportunity, please submit your cover letter and resume as one document via KPU\u2019s Career Centre. \u00a0Resume review will be conducted on October 16, 2026 however, the competition will remain open until filled. For inquiries or recommendations related to this position, please contact: Evita Gandhi Talent Acquisition Specialist Email: evita.gandhi@kpu.ca Salary Information The above compensation range is the span between the minimum and maximum base salary for a position. \u00a0Typically, initial salary placement is approximately halfway between the minimum and the maximum. \u00a0This represents an employee that possesses full job knowledge, qualifications and experience for the position. \u00a0In the normal course, employees will be hired, transferred or promoted between the minimum and approximately halfway of the salary range for a job with consideration given to internal equity. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4828": {"title": "Welder Testing Support", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Welder Testing Support Department/Faculty Faculty of Trades & Technology Home Campus (Location) Cloverdale Tech - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 1 year Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4828 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to the Welder Testing Coordinator. SUMMARY The Student Assistant, Welder Testing Support provides general operational assistance in support of KPU welder testing. The role supports preparation of materials, maintenance of workspaces, and basic logistical tasks that contribute to program delivery, and shop readiness. Work is routine in nature and aligned with foundational skills taught within the program, with tasks completed under supervision and in accordance with established safety procedures. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Prepare materials and resources for instructional activities and student assessments. Support setup, organization, and basic cleaning of shop and workspace areas for welder testing. Complete routine entry-level preparation tasks aligned with program coursework (e.g., material or coupon preparation). Provide logistical support during testing, as directed. Monitor basic supply needs and report issues to instructional staff. Follow all safety procedures, including appropriate PPE and tool usage. QUALIFICATIONS Active student within a relevant trades program at the Faculty of Trades and Technology. Familiarity with shop safety practices and appropriate PPE usage through coursework. Ability to perform routine hands-on tasks in a shop environment. Reliable, organized, and able to manage time within scheduled shifts. Demonstrates attention to detail and willingness to support team operations. Able to follow instructions and work both independently and collaboratively. Physically able to perform light material handling and shop support activities. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4443": {"title": "Welding Instructor", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Welding Instructor Department/Faculty Faculty of Trades & Technology Home Campus (Location) Cloverdale Tech - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 1 (one) year on call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4443 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Faculty Pay Scale Employment Type: Qualified Faculty List Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Faculty (Kwantlen Faculty Association) Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): WELDING INSTRUCTOR POSITION TYPE: Qualified Faculty List POSITION START: As soon as possible FACULTY OVERVIEW: Kwantlen Polytechnic University\u2019s Welding program provides students with the necessary training to become professional welders. Students will develop the skill and knowledge to work safely and effectively in today\u2019s demanding industrial environment. POSITION OVERVIEW: The Faculty of Trades and Technology is currently seeking a Non-regular Type 1 Welding Instructor to provide short-term delivery of Apprenticeship Levels 1, 2, and 3, Welding Foundation and/or Levels B and A which may extend from a single day to several weeks. More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: British Columbia Certificate of Qualification with Interprovincial Red Seal Endorsement. Current BC Pipe Welder Pressure Vessel 7 (PWP7) and BC Pipe Welder Pressure Vessel 10 (PWP10) pressure tickets, or equivalent. A minimum of five years\u2019 experience working in the industry as a journeyperson. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates will be required to undergo a Criminal Record Check. *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. This competition is for successful candidates to be added to our Qualified Faculty List. When work in this area becomes available, our faculty will draw on our Qualified Faculty List to assign work, please indicate on your application your preferred workload percentage. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4800": {"title": "Wilson School of Design Student Assistant (Generalist with Specializations)", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Wilson School of Design Student Assistant (Generalist with Specializations) Department/Faculty Wilson School of Design Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration 6.5 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4800 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 3 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to the Wilson School of Design Dean\u2019s Office. SUMMARY The Student Assistant supports a range of activities within the Wilson School of Design (WSD), contributing to student success, operations, and community engagement. This role is designed as a flexible, multi-functional position, where students may work across different areas or be assigned a primary specialization based on skills, experience, and operational needs. Student Assistants play a key role in fostering a welcoming, inclusive, and dynamic environment by supporting student learning, events, communications, labs, and peer engagement initiatives. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. The following positions are available: Events & Communication Support : 2 vacancies Labs and Technical/Studio Support: 2 vacancies (Workshop) 2 vacancies (Studios and Production Labs) 1 vacancy (Textiles Lab) Applicants are required to indicate their interest in one (or more) of the above positions. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Core Responsibilities (All Student Assistants): Represent WSD as a positive, professional ambassador at events and within the community. Provide excellent customer service and respectful, timely support to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Assist with general operational tasks including setup, coordination, and logistics. Support promotion and communication of WSD activities and resources. Maintain organized, safe, and welcoming environments across spaces and activities. Work both independently and collaboratively while managing time effectively. Attend training sessions, team meetings, and professional development opportunities as required. Perform additional related duties as assigned. AREAS OF SPECIALIZATION Student Assistants will be assigned to one of the following streams and may be asked to support in other streams if needed. 1. Peer Mentorship & Student Engagement Under the supervision and direction of the Dean's Office designate: Provide peer support, guidance, and mentorship to students. Share information about academic resources, student services, and wellness supports. Foster a sense of belonging and community among WSD students. Participate in outreach, community-building initiatives, and student engagement 2. Events & Communications Support Under the supervision and direction of the Dean's Office designate: Assist with planning, coordination, and execution of events (e.g., recruitment, community, student life). Support event logistics including setup, takedown, and on-site coordination. Engage with current and prospective students and external community members. Contribute to the promotion and documentation of events (photography/video/social media) for web platforms. 3. Labs & Technical/Studio Support Under the supervision and direction of the Dean's Office designate: Provide general support for lab, workshop, and studio activities. Assist with non-specialized preparation and set-up tasks for classes, projects, and events. Help communicate established procedures and direct students to appropriate resources. Assist with tours, exhibitions, displays, installations, and special events. Observe and report equipment, facility, or safety concerns to supervisory staff. Support equipment use and lab operations that are supportive in nature. QUALIFICATIONS Currently enrolled student at the Wilson School of Design. Strong oral and written communication and interpersonal skills. Organized, reliable, self-motivated, and detail-oriented. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Comfortable engaging with diverse audiences and communities. Interest in student life, community engagement, or design environments. Assets (vary by specialization): Experience with events, communications, or social media. Experience in peer mentoring or leadership roles. Familiarity with lab equipment, tools, or creative production processes. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office, Adobe Creative Cloud, and WordPress. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree \u2013 BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4850": {"title": "Biology Instructor, NR2", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Biology Instructor, NR2 Department/Faculty Faculty of Science Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 1 Year Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4850 Internal Closing Date: October 29, 2026 External Closing Date: October 29, 2026 # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Faculty Pay Scale Employment Type: Faculty Contract Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Faculty (Kwantlen Faculty Association) Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ANATOMY AND PHYSIOLOGY INSTRUCTOR POSITION TYPE: NR 2 (50%) POSITION START: January 1, 2027 FACULTY OVERVIEW: As Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is the fourth largest university in the province of British Columbia and serves communities in the South Fraser region and beyond. A Leader in innovative education with a teaching-focused mandate, KPU offers all learners opportunities to achieve the highest standards of academic performance. Within KPU, the Faculty of Science has over 1,500 full-time students and over 200 faculty members and instructors from across the natural and applied sciences. Faculty of Science includes nine departments and over 30 programs at the undergraduate level, with offerings at all four KPU campuses. The faculty is also home to Canada Research Chair: Dr. Cayley Velazquez and Sherman Jen Research Chair, Dr. Paul Adams. The Faculty of Science offers experiential learning through hands-on curriculum and co-ops and research collaboration opportunities with KPU\u2019s Institute for Sustainable Horticulture (ISH), Institute of Sustainable Food Systems (ISFS), and Applied Genomics Center (AGC). As well, our faculty is home to over a hectare of horticulture field lab and working farm and a state-of-the art brewery, which has been recognized internationally and locally, winning BC Brewery of the Year in 2019. For more information about the Faculty of Science, please visit our website at: kpu.ca/science POSITION OVERVIEW: Kwantlen Polytechnic University\u2019s Faculty of Science is currently seeking applications for a 50% non-regularized (NR2) position to teach anatomy and physiology courses (BIOL1160 and BIOL1260 Anatomy and Physiology I and II) in spring and summer semesters. More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: Successful candidates will possess, at a minimum, a Master\u2019s degree (Ph.D. preferred) in an appropriate field of biology with demonstrated excellence in teaching anatomy and physiology at the post-secondary level with a hybrid delivery method. The successful applicant must have excellent written and oral communication skills in order to teach effectively in English. Expertise teaching other general biology or health science related courses will also be an asset. Those interested in applying can find more information on our courses by visiting our program websites at: BSc: Major in Biology | Kwantlen Polytechnic University and Health Science | KPU.ca - Kwantlen Polytechnic University . APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates are asked to submit: Statement of teaching philosophy (maximum one page) Description of how you will incorporate your research, professional experience and/or network to support undergraduate teaching (maximum one page) Current curriculum vitae that includes information about previous courses taught and relevant research, scholarly, or professional experience Evidence of undergraduate teaching success (e.g., peer and student reviews) Names of three referees willing to comment on your ability to contribute to a degree-granting Biological and Health Sciences department Please forward your application package with cover letter *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. This competition is for a maximum FTE of 50% (NR2). When possible, priority will be given to the candidate(s) who can maximize the FTE either individually, or collectively, as such please indicate on your application your preferred workload percentage. This competition could also be used to add candidates to our Qualified Faculty List, therefore also please indicate on your application if you are interested in being added to this list. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4816": {"title": "Degree Advisor", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Degree Advisor Department/Faculty Wilson School of Design Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration 12 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4816 Internal Closing Date: October 24, 2026 External Closing Date: October 28, 2026 # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 13 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $33.88 to $37.81 per hour Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Hours of Work (BCGEU): 8:30am - 4:30pm Hours per Week (BCGEU): 35 We are currently seeking a Degree Advisor to join our Wilson School of Design team. Job Overview Degree Advisors in the academic Faculties engage in collaborative practice to enhance the development, progression and retention of KPU students. Through guidance and the use of leading and innovative practices, Degree Advisors empower students to ensure student success. Degree Advisors also play a key role in the development and delivery of programs offered within the Faculty by providing advice and recommendations to the Dean and Faculty Chairs/Coordinators on alignment with student needs/interests and smooth degree completion. Education and Experience Successful completion of an undergraduate degree (Masters preferred) in a related area from an accredited university. A minimum of five years employment in a related position, preferably at a post-secondary institution. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated in-depth knowledge of the curricular nature of Faculty-specific degree programs and their development. Demonstrated in-depth knowledge of educational or career advancements available to Faculty-specific degree graduates including admission requirements to graduate studies and common professional certificate or other post-secondary programs. Demonstrated in-depth knowledge of secondary and post-secondary educational systems. Superior communication skills in English, both spoken and written, exhibiting a high level of tact, professionalism, and diplomacy. Superior inter-personal skills, with the ability to patiently and effectively deal with a diverse range of people in a respectful and professional manner. Demonstrated advocacy roles with diverse populations. Demonstrated ability to establish positive and productive working relationships with internal and external stakeholders at a variety of administrative levels. Proven ability to work cooperatively and constructively in a team environment, particularly in developing strategies for effective processes that require coordination between various departments in an organizational environment. Demonstrated experience in developing and delivering effective training activities and workshops for students related to Faculty-specific degree advising. Demonstrated experience in planning and presenting recruitment and marketing workshops and activities. Demonstrated ability to address confidential matters and materials with tact and discretion. Proven ability to comprehend, communicate and comply with established policies, practices and procedures. Superior accuracy and attention to detail, particularly in editing and interpreting documents. Superior time-management skills in coordinating projects and meeting multiple overlapping deadlines. Demonstrated ability to measure and recommend strategies promoting student success. Proven ability to successfully recognize, analyze and resolve problems; to work independently and establish own priorities; to exercise a high level of initiative and responsibility; and, to adapt quickly to new technologies and ongoing organizational transitions. Ability to work from all KPU campuses with flexibility for day and evening shifts; and, the ability to travel within Canada. Demonstrated competency at an intermediate level in various software including MS Word, MS Excel, and Power \u00a0 Point, internet browsers and email. Experience using student information management systems. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4841": {"title": "Director, Information Security", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Director, Information Security Department/Faculty IT Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration Permanent Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4841 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 14 \u2013 Administrative Salary Grid - $114,071 to $174,909 Employment Type: Permanent Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Frequent travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Administration/Management Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): We are currently seeking a strategic and forward-thinking Director, Information Security to join our Information Technology (IT) team! This is an exciting opportunity to lead KPU's enterprise cybersecurity program and help shape the future of information security across a dynamic, multi-campus institution. Job Overview Reporting to the Chief Information Officer, this senior leadership role oversees a team responsible for information security technologies and incident management while providing strategic direction for the protection of the University's systems, data, and digital services. The Director is responsible for advancing KPU's cybersecurity strategy, policies, controls, and programs that safeguard the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of KPU's information assets. Working closely with IT leaders and academic departments across KPU, the Director translates organizational priorities and risk requirements into practical security strategies and technical solutions. This role balances security, innovation, agility, and operational effectiveness while leading initiatives that strengthen KPU's overall security posture. This is an exciting opportunity to lead impactful security projects, influence enterprise-wide decision-making, and help shape the future of cybersecurity at KPU. From advancing incident response capabilities and cyber resilience to implementing new technologies, processes, and best practices, the Director will play a critical role in helping KPU navigate a complex environment. At KPU, you'll have the opportunity to make a meaningful impact while working in a collaborative, purpose-driven environment that values innovation, continuous learning, work-life balance, and employee well-being. If you're passionate about building strong security programs, leading high-performing teams, and driving meaningful change, we'd love to hear from you! Education and Experience Bachelor\u2019s degree in information system; A minimum of seven years of IT experience, with five years in an information security role and at least two years in a supervisory capacity; Certified Information Systems Security Professional (CISSP)information security is preferred; Or an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Proven expertise in Identifying, assessing, and prioritizing information security risks. Implement risk mitigation measures and ensure compliance with relevant regulations and standards. Strong leadership persuasion abilities and experience working with the risk management team and a variety of diverse business units. Strong project management skills and experience in creating and managing complex project plans, including budgeting and resource allocation. Demonstrated experience working with security tools, technologies, mechanisms and policy to support and protect business information infrastructure in a large organization. An understanding of operating system internals and network protocols. \u00a0Familiarity with the principles of cryptography and cryptanalysis. Knowledge and experience in developing and documenting security architecture and plans, including strategic, tactical and project plans. Experience developing and maintaining policies, procedures, standards and guidelines using a consultative and inclusive approach. Experience with common information security management frameworks. Experience in application technology security testing (white box, black box and code review) and in system technology security testing (vulnerability scanning and penetration testing). Familiarity with applicable legal and regulatory requirements for post-secondary education in the Province of British Columbia. Proven ability to communicate security technical concepts to nontechnical people to enhance understanding and drive decisions that lead to positive outcomes. Proficiency in performing risk, business impact, control, and vulnerability assessments, and in defining treatment of strategies. Excellent verbal, written and interpersonal communication skills, including the ability to communicate effectively with the IT organization, project and application development teams, management and business personnel and other internal and external University stakeholders. Ability to travel between campuses is required. Competencies Leadership: KPU employees inspire, coach, mentor, and support students, employees and KPU as a whole in achieving objectives. Accountability: KPU employees demonstrate fiscal accountability and take ownership for their actions, decisions and results. Continuous Improvement: KPU employees take a creative approach to opportunities, exploring unique ways to create optimal value for the KPU community. Collaboration: KPU employees work in functional and cross-functional teams, coming together to solve complex issues and accomplish objectives that will benefit the KPU community. Salary Information The above compensation range is the span between the minimum and maximum base salary for a position. Typically, initial salary placement is approximately halfway between the minimum and the maximum. This represents an employee that possesses full job knowledge, qualifications and experience for the position. In the normal course, employees will be hired, transferred or promoted between the minimum and approximately halfway of the salary range for a job with consideration given to internal equity. Want to know more? Click here to view the full job description. Application Process To apply for this opportunity, please submit your cover letter and resume as one document via KPU\u2019s Career Centre. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4851": {"title": "Officer - Scheduling", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Officer - Scheduling Department/Faculty Student Services - Registrar's Office Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 6 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4851 Internal Closing Date: October 24, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 9 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $30.34 to $33.88 per hour Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Hours of Work (BCGEU): 8:30am - 4:30pm Hours per Week (BCGEU): 35 We are currently seeking an Officer - Scheduling to join our Scheduling & Registration team. Job Overview The Officer - Scheduling is responsible for the timely, efficient and accurate scheduling of KPU's post-secondary, apprenticeship, and continuing education class timetables, including final exam schedules. The incumbent works cooperatively with Dean's Office staff to build complex timetable schedules and problem-solving scheduling issues. The role creates and updates the details of course sections in the student information system, assigns rooms to in-person sections, which results in published term timetables. This allows for both online and back-office student registration to occur each term. Education and Experience A bachelor's degree. Minimum of one (1) year recent related experience in academic scheduling within the Office of the Registrar or post-secondary institution. Or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Experience using an enterprise student information system, ideally using a class schedule module. Beginner level experience using an academic room scheduling system. Intermediate level experience using Microsoft Excel. Beginner level experience with Microsoft Office Suite or productivity software. Microsoft Office certification an asset. Beginner level experience using an enterprise database reporting tool to produce operational and audit reports from a relational database. Demonstrated knowledge of Canadian post-secondary education systems as it pertains to academic programs, policies and procedures. Excellent oral and written communication skills including the ability to present information in a clear and concise manner. Ability to interact effectively with a variety of individuals with diverse backgrounds and needs. Demonstrated ability to deal with sensitive situations that call for the use of diplomacy, tact and professionalism in the delivery of information and explanations. Excellent organizational and time management skills, demonstrated attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to take initiative and work independently. Proven ability to juggle and prioritize tasks, work to deadlines and demands, make responsible decisions and determine when to seek advice. Ability to respond well to working under pressure and resolve complex issues in an effective manner. Demonstrate problem solving, needs analysis and analytical skills. Ability to think creatively while carrying out existing activities, keeping a process improvement perspective in mind. Demonstrated interpersonal skills to work collaboratively as an effective team player with all levels of the organization. Proven ability to exercise tact, diplomacy, and conflict resolution. Ability to provide guidance, direction, training and education to others. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4824": {"title": "Provost & Vice President, Academic", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Provost & Vice President, Academic Department/Faculty Office of the Provost & VP, Academic Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 5 YEAR TERM Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4824 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 19 \u2013 Administrative Salary Grid - $182,817 to $280,319 Employment Type: Permanent Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Frequent travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Administration/Management Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): Reporting directly to KPU\u2019s President and Vice Chancellor, the Provost and Vice President, Academic is the University\u2019s senior academic officer, providing leadership for academic programs and services, applied research, faculty relations, and the broader educational mission. Working collaboratively across the University, the Provost will lead the development and implementation of KPU\u2019s Academic Plan, champion exceptional student learning experiences, and advance KPU\u2019s identity as Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university. The successful candidate will bring a compelling vision that connects academic excellence with workforce and community relevance, expands access while ensuring educational quality, and links applied research and innovation with experiential and work-integrated learning. As Provost and Vice President, Academic, you will: Serve as the President\u2019s principal advisor on academic matters, contribute to KPU\u2019s executive leadership and strategic direction, keep the President informed of significant academic matters, and act on their behalf when required. Lead the development, implementation, and ongoing advancement of KPU\u2019s Academic Plan, aligning academic priorities with the University\u2019s vision and strategic objectives. Provide executive leadership across Faculties and Schools, teaching and learning, applied research and innovation, and library services, fostering collaboration across campuses, academic units, and administrative areas. Champion exceptional student learning experiences through the development, evaluation, and renewal of high-quality, relevant, and responsive programs, curricula, and services, advancing innovation in teaching, instructional delivery, and educational technology. Advance applied research and innovation that strengthen teaching, learning, scholarship, and KPU\u2019s polytechnic mandate. Collaborate with Senate and its committees on academic priorities, policies, programs, curricula, and governance; support the Board of Governors and its committees and implement Board decisions within the academic portfolio. Lead and mentor a diverse academic leadership team, establishing clear goals and empowering leaders while working with Deans and academic leaders to recruit, retain, develop, and support outstanding faculty and employees. Partner with the Office of Planning and Accountability, Deans, FSO, International, and other institutional leaders to support sustainable domestic and international enrolment. Lead academic resource planning, including program profiles, operating and capital budgets, and responsible resource allocation across the academic portfolio. Support effective employee and labour relations by applying KPU\u2019s collective agreements and partnering with Labour Relations and academic leaders on complex workplace matters. Represent KPU with government ministries, post-secondary partners, school boards, and community organizations, and through provincial, national, and international initiatives. Ensure that anti-racism, justice, equity, diversity, and inclusion inform the institution\u2019s decision-making and positively impact cultural and learning environments, and support the implementation of KPU\u2019s Task Force on Anti-racism, the Accessibility Plan, and the EDI Action Plan.[ Foster strong relationships with Indigenous leaders and communities and guide KPU\u2019s implementation of the Truth and Reconciliation Commission of Canada: Calls to Action; the President shall support the development and implementation of KPU\u2019s Indigenization Strategy What You bring: You are an accomplished and forward-thinking academic leader with demonstrated credibility as an educator, scholar, and senior administrator. You bring a deep understanding of the complexity of leading within a university environment and the proven ability to balance academic values, institutional priorities, governance, financial stewardship, and the changing needs of students and communities. You are a principled, collaborative, and consultative leader with exceptional communication, interpersonal and relationship-building skills. You inspire confidence and foster a culture of accountability, innovation and shared purpose. With demonstrated success leading organizational change in large, complex institutions, you bring strong change management capabilities and the ability to navigate uncertainty and guide people through significant transitions. You are a leader with integrity, sound judgment, transparency, and respect, and a proven track record of building trust, fostering meaningful engagement, and the ability to build consensus while navigating organizational challenges. You bring people together across academic and institutional boundaries to advance KPU\u2019s mission and strengthen its distinctive polytechnic identity opportunities. We\u2019re looking for someone who: Holds a doctorate and brings a minimum of 10 years of progressive, relevant post-secondary leadership and administrative experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Brings five to seven years of university faculty experience and strong academic credibility demonstrated through excellence in teaching and scholarship. Has held significant academic leadership responsibilities, ideally as a Provost, Vice President, Dean, or in a comparable senior academic leadership role. Has experience working within a complex, unionized public-sector environment. Brings comprehensive experience across the responsibilities of a senior academic portfolio, including academic planning, budgeting and resource allocation, Senate and academic governance, faculty recruitment and development, and program planning. Has successfully led the development and implementation of an Academic Plan and translated institutional strategy into clear academic priorities and outcomes. Demonstrates the ability to lead significant organizational change, engage diverse communities, and mentor and develop senior leaders, through a collaborative, transparent, and inclusive approach. Understands the role of applied research within a teaching-focused polytechnic university and the supports required to strengthen applied research and innovation. Brings deep knowledge of pedagogy, educational leadership, academic administration, and emerging trends in post-secondary education, learning design, and technology. Has strong business and financial acumen and supports evidence-based decision-making, accountability, and responsible resource stewardship. Has demonstrated success working collaboratively within a multi-union environment and navigating complex labour and employee relations matters. Understands and can articulate the distinctive value of polytechnic education, connecting academic excellence and intellectual inquiry with applied learning, workforce relevance, and community impact. Is an exceptional communicator and listener with an accessible, consultative leadership style and the diplomacy and judgment required to navigate complex institutional issues. Demonstrates a high level of integrity, credibility, sound judgment, political acuity, and resourcefulness. Understands Indigenous perspectives and priorities, with experience advancing decolonization through curriculum, policy, teaching, learning, and the broader work of the University, while demonstrating a sustained commitment to reconciliation. Demonstrates intercultural understanding and a strong commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, accessibility and belonging. Is deeply committed to students, their learning, and the transformative role of post-secondary education. For more detailed information on this position, click here . The Location KPU is a multi-campus institution. The Provost Office is located on Surrey campus, however, frequent travel between campuses will be required. Application Process To apply for this opportunity, please submit your cover letter and resume as one document via KPU\u2019s Career Centre. \u00a0Resume review will be conducted on November 10, 2026 , however, the competition will remain open until filled. For inquiries related to this position, please contact: Evita Gandhi Talent Acquisition Specialist Email: evita.gandhi@kpu.ca Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4843": {"title": "Senior Information Security Analyst", "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Senior Information Security Analyst Department/Faculty IT Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration PERMANENT Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada\u2019s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC\u2019s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4843 Internal Closing Date: October 24, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 15-12 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $42.35 to $46.55 per hour Employment Type: Permanent Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Hours of Work (BCGEU): 8:30am - 4:30pm Hours per Week (BCGEU): 35 We are currently seeking a Senior Information Security Analyst to join our Information Technology (IT) team. Job Overview The Senior Information Security Analyst is a senior position responsible for providing leadership, technical guidance, recommending and implementing security controls to safeguard KPU\u2019s valuable information assets. The analyst will also act as a liaison and work with all KPU business units as well as tactical hands-on resources in IT operations including incident detection and response. The position reports directly to the Director of Information Security. Priority consideration will be given to BCGEU employees currently impacted by layoff at the same or lower pay grade. Education and Experience Completion of a college or university diploma/degree in computing studies supplemented by 5 + years\u2019 progressive experience in an Information Security related field with demonstrated experience related to IT security, auditing and compliance functions. Experience leading planning/implementation major IT \u00a0projects. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Comprehensive general understanding of information risk concepts and principles, as a means of relating business needs to security controls. Understanding of key trends and players in the Information Security industry, particularly with respect to enterprise solutions, and cloud based technologies. Demonstrated knowledge of Operating System patch management tools Good understanding of Active Directory User and Group administration. Knowledge of the fundamentals of project management, and experience with creating and managing project plans, including budgeting and resource allocation. Good understanding of risk assessment methods and technologies. Some proficiency in performing risk, business impact, control and vulnerability assessments. Superior organizational skills with the ability to set priorities, follow-up and ability to manage multiple concurrent initiatives to meet challenging deadlines. Ability to research, evaluate and plan the implementation of emerging technology. Excellent technical knowledge of Microsoft Windows desktop and server operating systems and a wide range of security technologies, such as network security appliances, identity and access management (IAM) systems, anti-malware solutions, automated policy compliance tools, and desktop security tools. Excellent verbal and written communications skills and well developed interpersonal skills Ability to work under minimal supervision, under own initiative and as an effective team leader. Ability to independently organize work to achieve predetermined goals and meet deadlines. Knowledge in developing, documenting and maintaining information security policies, processes, procedures and standards. Knowledge of network infrastructure, including routers, switches, firewalls, and the associated network protocols and concepts. Strong analytical skills to analyze security requirements and relate them to appropriate security controls. Ability to interact with KPU's personnel at all levels and across all business units. Demonstrated leadership abilities, with the capability to develop and work within an information security team. A strong customer/client focus, with the ability to manage expectations appropriately, to provide a superior customer/client experience and build long-term relationships. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU\u2019s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"}}, "rows": {"https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4786": {"school_id": 1896, "posting_url": "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4786", "job_title_in_post": "Accounts Payable Clerk", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "August 30, 2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4835": {"school_id": 1896, "posting_url": "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4835", "job_titl